│                                                                    │
│  • Location 1: sphinx/ext/autodoc.py                               │
│     • Issue: The importlib.import_module call searches for         │
│       unqualified names in all submodules instead of the current   │
│       module and its parent modules.                               │
│     • Intended Behavior: Adjust the module path to include the     │
│       current module and its ancestors, ensuring unqualified names │
│       are resolved correctly.                                      │
│  • Location 2: sphinx/ext/autodoc.py                               │
│     • Issue: The module resolution logic does not prioritize the   │
│       current module and its parent modules for unqualified name   │
│       lookup.                                                      │
│     • Intended Behavior: Resolve unqualified names in the current  │
│       module and its parent modules, preserving existing           │
│       functionality.                                               │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                             📌 Summary                             │
│                                                                    │
│ The root cause is the module resolution logic in                   │
│ sphinx/ext/autodoc.py, which searches for unqualified names in all │
│ submodules instead of the current module and its parents. The fix  │
│ involves adjusting the module path to include the current module   │
│ and its ancestors, ensuring unqualified names are resolved         │
│ correctly.                                                         │
